  "response": "**Solution:**\n\nCount of numbers from 1–1000 divisible by 3 or 5:\n- Divisible by 3: ⌊1000/3⌋ = 333\n- Divisible by 5: ⌊1000/5⌋ = 200\n- Divisible by 15 (both): ⌊1000/15⌋ = 66\n- Divisible by 3 or 5: 333 + 200 − 66 = 467\n\nNow subtract those also divisible by 7 (i.e., divisible by 21 or by 35, since 21=3·7 and 35=5·7):\n- Divisible by 21: ⌊1000/21⌋ = 47\n- Divisible by 35: ⌊1000/35⌋ = 28\n- Divisible by 105 (lcm of 21,35, both): ⌊1000/105⌋ = 9\n- Divisible by 21 or 35: 47 + 28 − 9 = 66\n\nFinal count: 467 − 66 = **401**\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 401",
